{"name":"Eugenia","hex":"#f2e8d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Eugenia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Myrtaceae."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Ancient Greek. Variant: Eugenie.","45 Eugenia, a main belt asteroid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Eugenia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eugenia","blocks":[{"text":"Eugenia is a genus of flowering plants in the myrtle family Myrtaceae. It has a worldwide, although highly uneven, distribution in tropical and subtropical regions. The bulk of the approximately 1,100 species occur in the New World tropics, especially in the eastern Brazil's northern Andes, the Caribbean, and the Atlantic Forest. Other centers of diversity include New Caledonia and Madagascar. Many species in the Old World have received a new classification into the genus Syzygium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Eugenia1.jpg/330px-Eugenia1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugenia","wikidata":"Q975998"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"Eugenia":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/60/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Eugenia.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/60/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Eugenia.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Eugenia.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/60/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Eugenia.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Eugenia.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Blue-Beige Gradient","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Blue-Beige_Gradient.jpg/500px-Blue-Beige_Gradient.jpg","ratio":1.6,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blue-Beig